  "reason": "With no completed experiments, the key uncertainty is whether a simple RNA representation provides a useful performance baseline before adding learned encoders, multiprofile aggregation, or image fusion. config_001 tests the lowest-complexity RNA-only, single-profile PCA baseline, giving a cheap reference for validation accuracy and F1 while isolating the contribution of the RNA representation. It is the best first experiment under a limited budget because it establishes an anchor for later comparisons without confounding multiple design choices."
